Serverless? (Three different situations)

| Situation                             | Serverless? | Why                                               |
| ------------------------------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| Python running on your laptop         | ❌ No        | Your laptop provides the computing infrastructure |
| FastAPI running on EC2                | ❌ No        | You have a continuously running server            |
| Python function running on AWS Lambda | ✅ Yes       | AWS manages the underlying server infrastructure  |

============

The key idea

Serverless does NOT mean "there is no server."

There are servers behind AWS Lambda.

It means:

You don't have to manage those servers yourself.

That's why your simple a + b program can run perfectly without Lambda, but if you put the same logic inside Lambda, it becomes a serverless function.

